Hi,

Looks like differences between rjags and jagsUI (used more in the AHM book) are mucking things up.

out4J is a Jags model object, and coda::traceplot requires a call to an mcmc object (samples is an mcmc list).

If you fit the model using jagsUI with the call out4J <-jags(model.file="ANCOVA2.txt",data=win.data, inits,....[etc]), out4J is an object of class jagsUI, which is just what jagsUI::traceplot requires.

John

